.TH SDL_CreateAsyncIOQueue 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateAsyncIOQueue \- Create a task queue for tracking multiple I/O operations.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AsyncIOQueue * SDL_CreateAsyncIOQueue(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Async I/O operations are assigned to a queue when started\[char46] The queue can be checked for completed tasks thereafter\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a new task queue object or NULL if there was an error; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_DestroyAsyncIOQueue (3),
.BR SDL_GetAsyncIOResult (3),
.BR SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult (3)
